{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"I submitted the mitigation, but I'm not sure the cronjob I changed was what was degrading service for users.\n\nThe application looked healthy when I checked. All pods were running, and the frontend's search, recommendation, login and reservation requests returned 200 in a few milliseconds. The only fault I found was the `audit-log-archiver` CronJob, which runs every minute. Its `fluent-bit-sidecar` container never exits, so each job stays at 1/2 containers ready and never completes. With `concurrencyPolicy: Allow`, a new stuck job would pile up every minute.\n\nI patched the CronJob and deleted the two stuck jobs:\n- **Concurrency:** set `concurrencyPolicy` to `Forbid`.\n- **Cleanup:** added `activeDeadlineSeconds: 60` and `ttlSecondsAfterFinished: 120`, so a stuck job is killed after a minute and removed shortly after.\n\nI did not change the sidecar itself, so archiver jobs still won't complete normally. They will now end by hitting the 60-second deadline.\n\nI POSTed an empty `solution` to the submit endpoint once. It returned \"Submission received\"."}}
